    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d615">

                <pb facs="0664" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52—Agrarian Commission/27<hi
                        rendition="#superscript">3/7</hi>
                </note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8007</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-01-26">January 26,
                        1939</date>.<lb/>[Received January 31.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction no. 2335 of January 14, 1939, directing the
                    transmission to the Foreign Office of a note regarding statements attributed to
                    President Cárdenas, concerning agrarian affectations<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d615-f1"/> and compensation therefor.</p>
                <p>In compliance with the Department’s instructions, a note was sent to the Foreign
                    Office under date of January 16, 1939. This note was delivered personally by Mr.
                    Boal, at that time Chargé d’Affaires ad <pb facs="0665" n="657" xml:id="pg657"/>
                    interim, who made the remarks requested by the Department in its instruction
                    under reference. A copy of this Note is enclosed.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d615-f2"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>The Embassy is now in receipt of a note from the Foreign Office, dated January
                    19, 1939, a copy and translation of which are enclosed,<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d615-f3"/> in reply. The Embassy has made no acknowledgment of the
                    note, pending the receipt of further instructions from the Department.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
